          {
            "id": "s1:p1",
            "text": "Thymus mastichina is a species in the family Lamiaceae. It is endemic to the central Iberian Peninsula in Spain and Portugal."
          },
          {
            "id": "s1:p2",
            "text": "The perennial herb, with white flowers, can reach a height of {{convert|50|cm|ft|frac=2}}."
          },
          {
            "id": "s1:p3",
            "text": "Uses: Oil from the flower is used in some pain-relieving lotions, such as Aleve X."
